{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "the social network is a gripping drama that chronicles the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles faced by its creator, mark zuckerberg. directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, the film excels in its sharp dialogue and rapid pacing. jesse eisenberg delivers a standout performance as zuckerberg, portraying him as a brilliant but socially awkward individual driven by a desire for recognition and belonging. the supporting cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin and justin timberlake as sean parker, adds depth to the narrative of friendship, betrayal, and ambition. trent reznor and atticus ross provide an atmospheric electronic score that perfectly complements the cold, calculated tone of the story. visually, the movie uses dark lighting and tight framing to create a sense of isolation despite the theme of global connectivity. it is not just a biopic about a tech giant; it is a profound exploration of human relationships in the digital age. the film remains relevant years after its release, offering a critical look at how social media has reshaped society. overall, the social network is a masterpiece of modern cinema that combines excellent storytelling with technical brilliance.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.25193143}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.013670719}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " gripping", "logprob": -0.40242878}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.017208211}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.027727611}, {"token": " chron", "logprob": -0.0010549028}, {"token": "icles", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.00012935045}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -4.5419773e-05}, {"t